#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
claude-export-unpack — Claude.ai chat export zips -> ONE MARKDOWN FILE PER
CONVERSATION, written under a directory ragnarok-corpus actually walks.

WHY THIS EXISTS. A Claude.ai data export arrives as a zip of JSON: one
75 MB `conversations.json` holding every chat, plus `design_chats/`,
`projects/`, `memories/`, `light_metadata/`. Nothing on this box can read
that. ragnarok-corpus walks ~ for TEXT, and `~/ingest` — where the zips
land — is in its SKIP_TOP, so his entire Claude chat history was invisible
to every local model and every retrieval on this machine. Unpacking it into
per-conversation markdown somewhere the walker goes is the whole job.

WHAT IS RENDERED, and what is not:
  conversations.json      -> one .md per conversation          RENDERED
  design_chats/*.json     -> one .md per design chat           RENDERED
  projects/, memories/, light_metadata/, anything else         SKIPPED, NAMED
Projects and memories are not conversations, so they are out of scope here —
but every skipped zip and member is printed in the run summary, because a
source dropped in silence teaches a reader a confident absence.

REDACTION IS STRUCTURAL, NOT REMEMBERED. Chat history is the most
credential-dense text on this box that nobody thinks of as credential-dense:
pasted tokens, MCP tool_result payloads, .env contents quoted into a
question. The output lands in a walked directory, so the very next
`ragnarok-corpus` run reads all of it — and that build REFUSES (exit 4) if a
live secret survives its sweep. So every rendered document goes through
ragnarok-save's sweep first, IMPORTED, never copied: two copies of a
redaction list is one list that is wrong.
  - No ragnarok-save, or no live secrets loaded -> nothing is written. Fail
    closed; a redactor that is absent is not a redactor that passed.
  - A live value that survives redaction -> that ONE file is skipped and
    named loudly. The run is not abandoned: 300 clean conversations are not
    forfeit because one is dirty.
  - The TITLE is redacted before it becomes a filename. Metadata is output
    too (ragnarok-corpus learned that from a Config record whose primary
    field WAS the token).

EXPORTS ARE CUMULATIVE, SO THE SAME CONVERSATION ARRIVES AGAIN. Every
Claude.ai export contains the whole history, not the delta. Zips are therefore
collected across every source FIRST and deduplicated by conversation uuid,
keeping the copy with the newest `updated_at` — without that, the second export
he ever drops in writes a second file per conversation (the uuid8 in the stem
makes the names collide, and the collision suffix turns them into `-2.md`),
each one holding the OLDER version, and the state file then reports both as
unchanged forever. The count of conversations seen in more than one zip is
printed. If a conversation's TITLE changed between exports its old file is an
ORPHAN: that is reported with the exact `rm` for it and is NEVER deleted here —
this script does not remove files it did not just write.

THE FILENAME CAN UNDO THE WHOLE JOB, and this was measured, not imagined.
ragnarok-corpus refuses to OPEN any file whose NAME matches a credential
pattern — `(?i)credential`, `(?i)secret`, `.env`, `.pat`. Two of his chats are
titled "Handling credentials securely" and "Microsoft credential prefix", so
the first real run wrote 317 files and the corpus walked 315: the two most
security-relevant conversations were dropped, silently, by a rule meant for
`.env` files. The gate is therefore IMPORTED from the corpus and asked about
every filename before it is used; a slug word that trips it is dropped from
the NAME while the full title stays in the document's H1 and header. Never a
copy of the corpus's exclusion list — that would be a second list to keep
right. A missing corpus script degrades this to a printed warning, not a
failure: unpacking is the job, and the gate is an assurance on top of it.

MESSAGE ORDER. `parent_message_uuid` implies a tree, and branches are real —
regenerated/edited turns give two messages the same parent. Measured on the
2026-09-09 export: 22 of 313 conversations branch, and in ALL 313 the array
order equals created_at order. So messages are rendered in ARRAY ORDER, which
is chronological, and a conversation that branches SAYS SO in its header
instead of being silently flattened. No tree walker.

THE 1 MB LINE IS NOT COSMETIC. ragnarok-corpus tails any file over
MAX_FILE_BYTES (1,000,000) — it keeps the END and drops the head. A long chat
rendered as one 3 MB file would enter the corpus with its beginning missing
and nothing would say so, so oversized conversations are SPLIT at message
boundaries into `-part02.md`, each part carrying the same header.

USAGE
  claude-export-unpack                       # ~/ingest -> ~/claude-chats
  claude-export-unpack path/to/export.zip …  # explicit zips and/or dirs
  claude-export-unpack --dry-run             # render, redact, count; write nothing
  claude-export-unpack --force               # re-render even if unchanged
  --out DIR          where the markdown goes (default ~/claude-chats)
  --tool-chars N     cap per tool_use/tool_result payload (0 = omit them)
  --thinking-chars N cap per thinking block (0 = omit them)
  --max-bytes N      split a conversation above this (default 900000)

Reruns are incremental: state is keyed on conversation uuid + updated_at and
lives in ~/.local/state/ragnarok/, NOT in the output directory — anything
non-markdown left there would itself be walked into the corpus.

Read-only apart from --out and its own state file. Exit 0 clean, 1 if some
file was skipped for surviving secrets, 2 if it could not run at all.
"""

import argparse, hashlib, importlib.machinery, importlib.util, json, os, re, sys, time, zipfile

HOME = os.path.expanduser("~")
OUT_DIR = os.environ.get("CLAUDE_EXPORT_OUT", os.path.join(HOME, "claude-chats"))
DEFAULT_SRC = os.environ.get("CLAUDE_EXPORT_SRC", os.path.join(HOME, "ingest"))
# ragnarok/ops/tools: the redaction copy sits next to this file; ~/scripts/ragnarok-save is the Alexus original
_HERE = os.path.dirname(os.path.realpath(__file__))
SAVE_SCRIPT = os.environ.get("CLAUDE_EXPORT_SAVE_SCRIPT") or next((p for p in (os.path.join(_HERE, "ragnarok-save"), os.path.join(HOME, "scripts", "ragnarok-save")) if os.path.exists(p)), os.path.join(_HERE, "ragnarok-save"))
STATE_DIR = os.environ.get("CLAUDE_EXPORT_STATE",
                           os.path.join(HOME, ".local", "state", "ragnarok"))
STATE_FILE = os.path.join(STATE_DIR, "claude-export-unpack.json")
CORPUS_SCRIPT = os.environ.get("CLAUDE_EXPORT_CORPUS_SCRIPT",
                               os.path.join(HOME, "scripts", "ragnarok-corpus", "compile.py"))

# Test seam, the git-history-scan shape: extra secret VALUES, one per line, so
# a fixture can prove a planted credential never reaches the output without
# ever touching this box's real tokens.
EXTRA_SECRETS_FILE = os.environ.get("CLAUDE_EXPORT_SECRETS_FILE", "")

MAX_BYTES = 900_000          # ragnarok-corpus tails anything over 1,000,000
SLUG_MAX = 60


def die(msg, code=2):
    print(f"claude-export-unpack: {msg}", file=sys.stderr)
    sys.exit(code)


def load_save_module():
    """Import ~/scripts/ragnarok-save for its redaction. It has no .py suffix and
    everything real is behind __main__, so importing runs nothing."""
    spec = importlib.util.spec_from_loader(
        "ragnarok_save", importlib.machinery.SourceFileLoader("ragnarok_save", SAVE_SCRIPT))
    mod = importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec)
    spec.loader.exec_module(mod)
    return mod


def load_corpus_gate():
    """A predicate: would ragnarok-corpus OPEN a file with this name? IMPORTED
    from the corpus itself, so its exclusion list stays in one place. Returns
    None when the corpus is not on this box — the caller degrades and says so."""
    try:
        spec = importlib.util.spec_from_file_location("ragnarok_corpus_compile", CORPUS_SCRIPT)
        mod = importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec)
        spec.loader.exec_module(mod)
        return lambda name: bool(mod.wanted_file(os.path.join(OUT_DIR, name), name))
    except Exception:                                               # noqa: BLE001
        return None


def corpus_safe_words(words, date, uuid8, gate):
    """Drop only the slug words that make the corpus refuse the file. The title
    is never altered — it stays in the H1 — this is the FILENAME alone."""
    def nm(ws):
        return f"{date}-{'-'.join(ws) or 'untitled'}-{uuid8}.md"
    if not gate or gate(nm(words)):
        return words, []
    kept = [w for w in words if gate(nm([w]))]
    dropped = [w for w in words if w not in kept]
    if not gate(nm(kept)):
        kept, dropped = [], list(words)
    return kept, dropped


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Rendering
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

def slugify(name):
    s = re.sub(r"[^a-z0-9]+", "-", (name or "").lower()).strip("-")
    return (s[:SLUG_MAX].rstrip("-") or "untitled")


def as_list(v):
    """Export fields are sometimes JSON-encoded strings and sometimes real lists."""
    if isinstance(v, str):
        try:
            v = json.loads(v)
        except Exception:
            return []
    return v if isinstance(v, list) else []


def cap(text, limit):
    text = text if isinstance(text, str) else json.dumps(text, ensure_ascii=False)
    if limit and len(text) > limit:
        return text[:limit] + f"\n… [{len(text) - limit:,} chars capped]", 1
    return text, 0


def render_blocks(msg, opts, stats):
    """Content blocks -> markdown. Falls back to the flattened `text` field when
    a message carries no parseable blocks (349 of 8,536 in the first export had
    an empty text field but real blocks, and a handful the reverse)."""
    out = []
    for b in as_list(msg.get("content")):
        if not isinstance(b, dict):
            continue
        t = b.get("type")
        if t == "text":
            if (b.get("text") or "").strip():
                out.append(b["text"])
        elif t == "thinking":
            if opts.thinking_chars == 0:
                stats["omitted_thinking"] += 1
                continue
            body, capped = cap(b.get("thinking") or "", opts.thinking_chars)
            stats["capped"] += capped
            if body.strip():
                out.append("**[thinking]**\n\n```\n" + body + "\n```")
        elif t == "tool_use":
            if opts.tool_chars == 0:
                stats["omitted_tools"] += 1
                continue
            body, capped = cap(b.get("input") or {}, opts.tool_chars)
            stats["capped"] += capped
            out.append(f"**[tool_use: {b.get('name') or '?'}]**\n\n```json\n{body}\n```")
        elif t == "tool_result":
            if opts.tool_chars == 0:
                stats["omitted_tools"] += 1
                continue
            body, capped = cap(b.get("content") or b.get("display_content") or "", opts.tool_chars)
            stats["capped"] += capped
            err = " (error)" if b.get("is_error") else ""
            out.append(f"**[tool_result: {b.get('name') or '?'}{err}]**\n\n```\n{body}\n```")
        elif t == "injected_prompt_block":
            body, capped = cap(b.get("prompt") or "", opts.tool_chars or 2000)
            stats["capped"] += capped
            if body.strip():
                out.append(f"**[injected prompt: {b.get('injection_source') or '?'}]**\n\n```\n{body}\n```")
        elif t in ("token_budget", "flag"):
            out.append(f"*[{t}: {b.get('remaining', b.get('flag', ''))}]*")
        else:
            out.append(f"*[unrendered block type: {t}]*")
            stats["unknown_blocks"] += 1

    if not out and (msg.get("text") or "").strip():
        out.append(msg["text"])

    # Attachments carry their extracted text IN FULL — a pasted file is the
    # substance of the turn, not decoration. `files` carries only a name.
    for a in as_list(msg.get("attachments")):
        if not isinstance(a, dict):
            continue
        name = a.get("file_name") or a.get("name") or "attachment"
        content = a.get("extracted_content") or a.get("content") or ""
        out.append(f"**[attachment: {name}]**\n\n```\n{content}\n```" if content
                   else f"*[attachment: {name} — no extracted text in the export]*")
    for f in as_list(msg.get("files")):
        if isinstance(f, dict):
            out.append(f"*[file: {f.get('file_name') or f.get('file_uuid') or '?'} — content not in the export]*")
    return "\n\n".join(out).strip()


def conversation_doc(conv, opts, stats, source):
    """One conversation -> (title, header, [message chunks])."""
    msgs = conv.get("chat_messages") or conv.get("messages") or []
    title = (conv.get("name") or conv.get("title") or "").strip()

    parents = {}
    for m in msgs:
        p = m.get("parent_message_uuid")
        if p:
            parents[p] = parents.get(p, 0) + 1
    branched = sum(n - 1 for n in parents.values() if n > 1)

    header = [
        f"# {title or '(untitled conversation)'}",
        "",
        f"- source: `{source}`",
        f"- uuid: `{conv.get('uuid', '')}`",
        f"- created: {conv.get('created_at', '')}",
        f"- updated: {conv.get('updated_at', '')}",
        f"- messages: {len(msgs)}",
    ]
    if branched:
        header.append(f"- branches: {branched} message(s) share a parent (edited or "
                      f"regenerated turns). Rendered in export array order, which is "
                      f"chronological; no branch was dropped and none is marked as the "
                      f"one that 'won'.")
    if conv.get("summary"):
        header.append(f"- summary: {conv['summary']}")
    header += ["", "---", ""]

    parts = []
    for m in msgs:
        # design_chats nest the real message under content{}: role, content, timestamp.
        inner = m.get("content") if isinstance(m.get("content"), dict) else None
        if inner is not None:
            sender = inner.get("role") or m.get("role") or "?"
            when = inner.get("timestamp") or m.get("created_at") or ""
            body = (inner.get("content") or "").strip()
            for a in inner.get("attachments") or []:
                if isinstance(a, dict) and (a.get("content") or "").strip():
                    body += (f"\n\n**[attachment: {a.get('name') or a.get('type') or '?'}]**"
                             f"\n\n```\n{a['content']}\n```")
        else:
            sender = m.get("sender") or m.get("role") or "?"
            when = m.get("created_at") or ""
            body = render_blocks(m, opts, stats)
        if not body:
            continue
        parts.append(f"## {sender} — {when}\n\n{body}\n")
    return title, "\n".join(header), parts


def split_parts(header, parts, max_bytes):
    """Pack message chunks into documents under max_bytes, splitting only at
    message boundaries. A single message bigger than the cap gets its own
    document rather than being cut mid-sentence."""
    docs, cur, size = [], [], 0
    for p in parts:
        if cur and size + len(p) > max_bytes:
            docs.append(cur); cur, size = [], 0
        cur.append(p); size += len(p)
    if cur:
        docs.append(cur)
    if not docs:
        docs = [[]]
    out = []
    for i, chunk in enumerate(docs, 1):
        note = "" if len(docs) == 1 else f"\n*(part {i} of {len(docs)} — split so ragnarok-corpus does not tail it)*\n"
        out.append(header + note + "\n" + "\n".join(chunk))
    return out


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Zip reading — by MEMBER SHAPE, never by filename. A design-components export
# sits in the same folder and is not chat.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

def zip_label(path):
    """Parent dir + filename. Every Claude.ai export is named `conversations-000.zip`,
    so the basename alone cannot tell two exports apart — and they land in dated
    folders precisely so a human can."""
    parent = os.path.basename(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(path)))
    return f"{parent}/{os.path.basename(path)}" if parent else os.path.basename(path)


def read_zip(path):
    """-> (conversations, skipped_members). Never extracts to disk."""
    convs, skipped = [], []
    with zipfile.ZipFile(path) as z:
        names = z.namelist()
        for n in names:
            if n.endswith("/"):
                continue
            base = os.path.basename(n)
            if n == "conversations.json":
                data = json.loads(z.read(n))
                for c in (data if isinstance(data, list) else [data]):
                    convs.append((c, f"{zip_label(path)}::conversations.json"))
            elif n.startswith("design_chats/") and n.endswith(".json"):
                c = json.loads(z.read(n))
                convs.append((c, f"{zip_label(path)}::{n}"))
            else:
                skipped.append((os.path.basename(path), n if len(n) < 80 else base))
    return convs, skipped


def gather_zips(sources):
    zips = []
    for s in sources:
        s = os.path.expanduser(s)
        if os.path.isdir(s):
            for root, dirs, files in os.walk(s):
                dirs[:] = sorted(dirs)
                zips += [os.path.join(root, f) for f in sorted(files) if f.lower().endswith(".zip")]
        elif os.path.isfile(s):
            zips.append(s)
        else:
            print(f"  ! not found, skipped: {s}")
    return zips


def main():
    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser(description="Claude.ai chat export zips -> per-conversation markdown")
    ap.add_argument("sources", nargs="*", default=[DEFAULT_SRC],
                    help=f"zip files and/or directories to scan (default {DEFAULT_SRC})")
    ap.add_argument("--out", default=OUT_DIR)
    ap.add_argument("--tool-chars", type=int, default=2000, help="cap per tool block; 0 omits them")
    ap.add_argument("--thinking-chars", type=int, default=4000, help="cap per thinking block; 0 omits them")
    ap.add_argument("--max-bytes", type=int, default=MAX_BYTES)
    ap.add_argument("--dry-run", action="store_true")
    ap.add_argument("--force", action="store_true", help="re-render conversations that have not changed")
    opts = ap.parse_args()
    sources = opts.sources or [DEFAULT_SRC]

    # Redaction first: no redactor, no output. An absent sweep is not a sweep
    # that passed, and this output lands where the corpus will read it.
    if not os.path.exists(SAVE_SCRIPT):
        die(f"{SAVE_SCRIPT} is missing — it owns the redaction sweep and this script "
            f"will not invent a second one. Nothing written.")
    try:
        save = load_save_module()
        _, secrets, srcs = save.collect_secrets()
        secrets = set(secrets)
    except Exception as e:                                          # noqa: BLE001
        die(f"could not load the redaction sweep ({type(e).__name__}: {e}) — refusing to "
            f"write chat history with only best-effort redaction. Nothing written.")
    if EXTRA_SECRETS_FILE and os.path.exists(EXTRA_SECRETS_FILE):
        extra = [l.strip() for l in open(EXTRA_SECRETS_FILE) if l.strip()]
        secrets |= set(extra)
        srcs = list(srcs) + [f"{len(extra)} from CLAUDE_EXPORT_SECRETS_FILE"]
    if not secrets:
        die("no live secret values loaded — the sweep would be blind to this box's own "
            "tokens. Fix the credential paths first. Nothing written.")
    print(f"claude-export-unpack: redaction armed — {len(secrets)} live value(s) from "
          f"{', '.join(srcs) or 'none'}, plus ragnarok-save's shape patterns")

    zips = gather_zips(sources)
    if not zips:
        die(f"no .zip found under: {', '.join(sources)}")

    state = {}
    if os.path.exists(STATE_FILE) and not opts.force:
        try:
            state = json.load(open(STATE_FILE)).get("conversations", {})
        except Exception:
            state = {}

    gate = load_corpus_gate()
    if gate is None:
        print(f"  ! {CORPUS_SCRIPT} not importable — filenames are NOT checked against "
              f"the corpus's own exclusion rules, so a chat titled about credentials may "
              f"be written and then never walked. Unpacking continues.")

    stats = {"capped": 0, "omitted_tools": 0, "omitted_thinking": 0, "unknown_blocks": 0}
    redactions, skipped_members, written, unchanged, dirty, oversize = {}, [], [], 0, [], []
    renamed = []
    chat_zips, non_chat_zips = [], []
    new_state, used_names = {}, {}

    if not opts.dry_run:
        os.makedirs(opts.out, mode=0o700, exist_ok=True)
        os.chmod(opts.out, 0o700)

    # Collect across every zip BEFORE rendering: the same conversation appears in
    # every export that covers its date, and the newest copy is the one to keep.
    collected, duplicates = {}, 0
    for zp in zips:
        try:
            convs, skipped = read_zip(zp)
        except (zipfile.BadZipFile, json.JSONDecodeError, KeyError) as e:
            non_chat_zips.append((os.path.basename(zp), f"unreadable: {type(e).__name__}"))
            continue
        if convs:
            chat_zips.append((os.path.basename(zp), len(convs)))
        else:
            non_chat_zips.append((os.path.basename(zp), f"no conversations.json / design_chats/ member "
                                                        f"({len(skipped)} other member(s))"))
        skipped_members += skipped

        for conv, source in convs:
            uuid = conv.get("uuid") or hashlib.sha256(json.dumps(conv, sort_keys=True).encode()).hexdigest()[:36]
            prev = collected.get(uuid)
            if prev is None:
                collected[uuid] = (conv, source)
            else:
                duplicates += 1
                if (conv.get("updated_at") or "") > (prev[0].get("updated_at") or ""):
                    collected[uuid] = (conv, source)

    for uuid, (conv, source) in collected.items():
        key = f"{uuid}:{conv.get('updated_at', '')}"
        title, header, parts = conversation_doc(conv, opts, stats, source)

        clean_title, found = save.redact(title, secrets)
        for k, v in found.items():
            redactions[k] = redactions.get(k, 0) + v
        date = (conv.get("created_at") or conv.get("updated_at") or "")[:10] or "undated"
        words, dropped_words = corpus_safe_words(
            slugify(clean_title).split("-"), date, uuid[:8], gate)
        if dropped_words:
            renamed.append((clean_title or "(untitled)", "-".join(dropped_words)))
        stem = f"{date}-{'-'.join(words) or 'untitled'}-{uuid[:8]}"
        n = used_names.get(stem, 0)
        used_names[stem] = n + 1
        if n:
            stem = f"{stem}-{n+1}"

        docs = split_parts(header, parts, opts.max_bytes)
        paths = [os.path.join(opts.out, stem + (".md" if i == 0 else f"-part{i+1:02d}.md"))
                 for i in range(len(docs))]
        new_state[uuid] = {"key": key, "files": [os.path.basename(p) for p in paths]}

        if state.get(uuid, {}).get("key") == key and not opts.force \
                and all(os.path.exists(p) for p in paths):
            unchanged += 1
            continue

        for path, body in zip(paths, docs):
            body, found = save.redact(body, secrets)
            for k, v in found.items():
                redactions[k] = redactions.get(k, 0) + v
            survivors = [s for s in secrets if s in body]
            if survivors:
                dirty.append(os.path.basename(path))
                new_state.pop(uuid, None)
                continue
            if len(body.encode()) > 1_000_000:
                oversize.append(os.path.basename(path))
            if not opts.dry_run:
                with open(path, "w") as fh:
                    fh.write(body)
                os.chmod(path, 0o600)
            written.append(os.path.basename(path))

    if not opts.dry_run:
        os.makedirs(STATE_DIR, mode=0o700, exist_ok=True)
        merged = dict(state); merged.update(new_state)
        with open(STATE_FILE, "w") as fh:
            json.dump({"updated": time.strftime("%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S%z"), "out": opts.out,
                       "conversations": merged}, fh, indent=1)
        os.chmod(STATE_FILE, 0o600)

    # -- summary. Everything not rendered is NAMED. ---------------------------
    print(f"\n{'DRY RUN — nothing written' if opts.dry_run else 'wrote'}: "
          f"{len(written)} markdown file(s) -> {opts.out}")
    print(f"  unchanged, skipped: {unchanged}")
    for name, n in chat_zips:
        print(f"  chat export: {name} — {n} conversation(s)")
    for name, why in non_chat_zips:
        print(f"  NOT a chat export, skipped: {name} — {why}")
    kinds = {}
    for zname, member in skipped_members:
        top = member.split("/")[0] if "/" in member else member
        kinds[f"{zname}::{top}"] = kinds.get(f"{zname}::{top}", 0) + 1
    for k in sorted(kinds):
        print(f"  member not rendered (not a conversation): {k} x{kinds[k]}")
    print(f"  redacted: {redactions or 'nothing matched'}")
    print(f"  blocks capped: {stats['capped']}, tool blocks omitted: {stats['omitted_tools']}, "
          f"thinking omitted: {stats['omitted_thinking']}, unknown block types: {stats['unknown_blocks']}")
    if duplicates:
        print(f"  same conversation seen in more than one zip: {duplicates} — kept the newest "
              f"copy of each (exports are cumulative, not deltas)")
    orphans = []
    for uuid, rec in state.items():
        if uuid in new_state:
            for old in rec.get("files", []):
                if old not in new_state[uuid]["files"] and os.path.exists(os.path.join(opts.out, old)):
                    orphans.append(old)
    if orphans:
        print(f"  ! ORPHAN(S) from an earlier run — the title changed, so these are the OLD "
              f"filenames for conversations that were just rewritten. Not deleted here:\n"
              f"      rm {' '.join(repr(os.path.join(opts.out, o)) for o in orphans)}")
    for title, words in renamed:
        print(f"  filename word(s) dropped so ragnarok-corpus will open the file "
              f"(its credential-name rule): '{words}' in \"{title}\" — the title is intact inside")
    if oversize:
        print(f"  ! still over 1 MB after splitting (ragnarok-corpus will TAIL these): {', '.join(oversize)}")
    if dirty:
        print(f"  !! SKIPPED — a live credential survived redaction in: {', '.join(dirty)}", file=sys.stderr)
        return 1
    return 0


if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main())
